1
00:00:05,989 --> 00:00:09,559
Heiwa Fansubs Presents:
"Great Detective Conan"
"Challenge to Kudo Shin'ichi"

2
00:00:09,860 --> 00:00:11,928
Oi, this is bad!

3
00:00:12,929 --> 00:00:15,032
This is the sort of atmosphere
where you get an explosion!

4
00:00:15,098 --> 00:00:16,700
Shin'ichi, hurry and remember!

5
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:17,868
I know!

6
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:19,970
Tea. Tea...

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:25,108
Oi!

8
00:00:32,115 --> 00:00:33,583
"When was the day you last drank tea?"

9
00:00:35,852 --> 00:00:38,355
Oh, that was close, that was close.

10
00:00:38,889 --> 00:00:41,258
Shin'ichi, did you remember?

11
00:00:41,591 --> 00:00:43,960
It'd be impossible to remember a date like that.

12
00:00:44,161 --> 00:00:46,096
Anyhow, it was just luck,
wasn't it, boy detective?

13
00:00:46,163 --> 00:00:47,831
No, you're wrong.

14
00:00:47,998 --> 00:00:50,200
I didn't input anything.

15
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:51,535
Eh?

16
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,471
Then, who...

17
00:00:55,038 --> 00:00:56,540
Damn!

18
00:00:58,408 --> 00:00:59,810
That's right...

19
00:01:00,444 --> 00:01:02,245
This date is...

20
00:01:02,446 --> 00:01:05,982
That sad incident that took place at...

21
00:01:06,483 --> 00:01:08,585
...the famous film director's villa.

22
00:01:08,952 --> 00:01:10,253
Ah...

23
00:01:11,988 --> 00:01:13,023
Shin'ichi's Childhood Friend
Mori Ran

24
00:01:13,056 --> 00:01:14,524
I never thought...

25
00:01:15,559 --> 00:01:19,696
...that you and I would get together like this.

26
00:01:23,233 --> 00:01:24,501
I love you.

27
00:01:25,635 --> 00:01:27,370
I want you.

28
00:01:28,805 --> 00:01:31,074
That's it, now kiss! A hot kiss!

29
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:34,544
Kiss?
That wasn't in the script, now was it?!

30
00:01:34,911 --> 00:01:36,546
Go with the flow, go with the flow.

31
00:01:36,713 --> 00:01:37,781
"Movie Director
Nagata Akihiro"

32
00:01:37,814 --> 00:01:40,083
This detective works by shaking up a
woman's heart while getting closer to the truth.

33
00:01:40,183 --> 00:01:42,018
That's why a kiss is essential.

34
00:01:42,085 --> 00:01:43,620
"Newcomer Actress - Ikusuki Saori"
Let's do it.

35
00:01:45,722 --> 00:01:47,891
High School Student Detective
Kudo Shin'ichi

36
00:01:47,958 --> 00:01:50,227
Hmmf. Why not do it?

37
00:01:50,360 --> 00:01:52,362
Fool. I couldn't do that.

38
00:01:52,429 --> 00:01:53,396
"Shin'ichi and Ran's Fellow Student
Suzuki Sonoko"

39
00:01:53,463 --> 00:01:55,165
What's wrong with a kiss?

40
00:01:55,365 --> 00:01:58,635
Director Nagata went to a lot of trouble
to direct your acting.

41
00:01:58,702 --> 00:02:02,305
Director Nagata is one of the
biggest directors in Japan, you know.

42
00:02:02,405 --> 00:02:05,375
So you shouldn't miss this chance!

43
00:02:05,475 --> 00:02:07,677
I'm not that big a deal.

44
00:02:08,845 --> 00:02:10,680
Hey, what's this "chance"?

45
00:02:10,747 --> 00:02:13,783
You said you wanted us to
keep you company for a play...

46
00:02:13,884 --> 00:02:15,886
...I certainly didn't hear anything about
asking Shin'ichi to take part in any love scenes.

47
00:02:15,952 --> 00:02:17,254
Then...

48
00:02:17,454 --> 00:02:20,857
Do you two want to give it a try?
A passionate love scene.

49
00:02:32,102 --> 00:02:34,137
Here you go.
Thank you very much.

50
00:02:34,204 --> 00:02:35,805
"Villa Manager
Ishihara Kana"

51
00:02:40,677 --> 00:02:43,446
Could it be you two haven't kissed?

52
00:02:48,618 --> 00:02:51,421
Here's how you kiss.

53
00:02:58,128 --> 00:02:59,529
Incredible...

54
00:03:04,034 --> 00:03:06,069
My, that is hot.

55
00:03:06,102 --> 00:03:08,705
"Actress
Nagata Chisato"

56
00:03:09,005 --> 00:03:12,142
Ah! It's the actress Nagata Chisato.

57
00:03:12,275 --> 00:03:13,843
Isn't she his wife?

58
00:03:13,910 --> 00:03:15,812
Chisato...

59
00:03:20,183 --> 00:03:22,319
You lied about shooting a film.

60
00:03:23,486 --> 00:03:26,856
As I thought, you were doing this.

61
00:03:29,359 --> 00:03:30,894
You thieving cat!

62
00:03:31,228 --> 00:03:36,066
When you use a person's husband like this,
you're a woman who's even below a thieving cat!

63
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,535
What are you doing?!

64
00:03:38,568 --> 00:03:41,338
If you can't manage your own husband,
then don't go shouting off your big mouth at me!

65
00:03:41,438 --> 00:03:43,340
I don't know if you're
all that great an actress...

66
00:03:43,673 --> 00:03:46,776
...but you got your roles
using your body, didn't you?!

67
00:03:47,444 --> 00:03:49,212
I won't allow this!

68
00:03:53,783 --> 00:03:56,419
If you can do it, go ahead and do it!

69
00:03:58,188 --> 00:04:02,092
Oi, oi, shape up already...

70
00:04:02,425 --> 00:04:04,594
Let it go, Chisato.

71
00:04:04,761 --> 00:04:08,732
Saori's my lover, so I'll be choosing her
for the lead in my next project.

72
00:04:08,898 --> 00:04:12,435
And you shouldn't let it
irritate you like this, now should you?

73
00:04:12,535 --> 00:04:16,640
It's been my ideal that my wife and lover
would be on good terms and get along together.

74
00:04:17,107 --> 00:04:22,445
The three of us should have fun
and live our lives fully... Right?

75
00:04:27,117 --> 00:04:30,253
Somehow...
this feels like the world of adults.

76
00:04:31,755 --> 00:04:34,424
I know, let's have tea! Right?

77
00:04:34,591 --> 00:04:37,594
I have some superb black tea.
Kana, please prepare it.

78
00:04:37,661 --> 00:04:38,928
Certainly.

79
00:04:39,029 --> 00:04:41,097
If you'd like, you guys can join us.

80
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,899
Ah, no...

81
00:04:43,099 --> 00:04:46,236
Of course we will. We'd love to.

82
00:04:49,706 --> 00:04:51,207
The pride of my collection.

83
00:04:51,274 --> 00:04:53,410
Venetian Meissen teacups...

84
00:04:53,476 --> 00:04:55,345
They're all world masterpieces.

85
00:04:56,313 --> 00:04:58,915
You guys can pick out any cup you'd like.

86
00:04:59,883 --> 00:05:02,752
These are dreamy, aren't they?
Which one will you pick?

87
00:05:02,952 --> 00:05:04,754
I'm not sure.

88
00:05:13,430 --> 00:05:17,267
Far greater than any play, you're the source
of some serious hurt, Director.

89
00:05:17,500 --> 00:05:19,669
You're saying some scary things.

90
00:05:19,836 --> 00:05:21,071
How about it?

91
00:05:21,271 --> 00:05:24,441
Wouldn't you like to
participate in my life, too?

92
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:29,446
I seriously can't follow this old guy.

93
00:05:30,447 --> 00:05:32,382
Are you still undecided?

94
00:05:33,316 --> 00:05:35,485
Shall I take this one?

95
00:05:35,585 --> 00:05:39,823
No, do I feel like this one today?

96
00:05:41,524 --> 00:05:43,093
What a nice fragrance.

97
00:05:43,226 --> 00:05:45,762
It's a Framboise tea made in Ceylon.

98
00:05:46,196 --> 00:05:48,698
Well then, let's enjoy our teatime.

99
00:05:49,065 --> 00:05:50,367
Just a minute.

100
00:05:52,869 --> 00:05:55,572
Your favorite Ponisshu sugar cubes...

101
00:05:57,474 --> 00:06:00,677
Whenever we have tea at home,
you always put one in, don't you?

102
00:06:01,978 --> 00:06:04,414
A thieving cat wouldn't know that.

103
00:06:04,547 --> 00:06:06,015
Didn't you just poison in it?

104
00:06:06,082 --> 00:06:07,717
Oh my.

105
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:10,653
The only thing I put in it was love.

106
00:06:13,223 --> 00:06:14,624
Right?

107
00:06:15,492 --> 00:06:16,793
Right?

108
00:06:18,762 --> 00:06:20,497
This is an interesting opening, isn't it?

109
00:06:20,597 --> 00:06:22,332
This is how it should have
looked from the beginning.

110
00:06:24,367 --> 00:06:26,436
Well then, let's start over.

111
00:06:30,039 --> 00:06:34,010
Life begins with a hot cup of tea.

112
00:06:34,878 --> 00:06:36,946
Itadakimasu.

113
00:06:43,787 --> 00:06:44,821
Dear!

114
00:06:44,921 --> 00:06:46,122
Director!

115
00:06:50,026 --> 00:06:52,495
Nagata-san! Nagata-san!

116
00:06:55,999 --> 00:06:57,667
He's dead...

117
00:07:03,206 --> 00:07:04,641
This is...

118
00:07:05,542 --> 00:07:07,243
...the odor of almonds.

119
00:07:07,377 --> 00:07:09,479
It's cyanide!

120
00:07:11,314 --> 00:07:12,749
No...

121
00:07:13,416 --> 00:07:14,984
It's a lie.

122
00:07:16,286 --> 00:07:18,655
Ma'am! Ma'am!

123
00:07:21,724 --> 00:07:23,960
Well then, if you would please.

124
00:07:25,228 --> 00:07:26,629
Please go back inside.

125
00:07:26,663 --> 00:07:29,699
Until the jurisdictional police arrive,
don't take even a single step out yet.

126
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:34,537
All of you are suspects
and also witnesses at the same time.

127
00:07:34,704 --> 00:07:36,306
Suspects?

128
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:41,277
Even you, the famous high school
student detective, are no exception.

129
00:07:42,412 --> 00:07:43,947
What's going on, Shin'ichi?

130
00:07:44,047 --> 00:07:46,216
Why are we being treated as suspects?

131
00:07:46,282 --> 00:07:49,986
You guys have gotten involved in
this terrible mess, too, haven't you?

132
00:07:50,220 --> 00:07:52,755
Well, me too, though.

133
00:07:54,324 --> 00:07:55,792
Judging from the situation...

134
00:07:55,892 --> 00:08:01,130
...it's apparent someone killed Director Nagata
by putting potassium cyanide into his tea.

135
00:08:02,198 --> 00:08:03,433
Problem is...

136
00:08:03,500 --> 00:08:08,972
...who was it and how did they get
the potassium cyanide into his tea?

137
00:08:09,205 --> 00:08:14,310
We first have to consider Manager Kana-san,
who brought in the tea.

138
00:08:14,944 --> 00:08:20,116
But Kana-san only brought in the one server
and poured tea to everyone from it.

139
00:08:20,183 --> 00:08:25,021
If the tea in the server did have
potassium cyanide in it...

140
00:08:25,288 --> 00:08:27,824
...then all of us here would have died.

141
00:08:28,191 --> 00:08:33,530
Could she have spread the cyanide beforehand
inside just the cup that Director Nagata used?

142
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:35,999
No, that would've been impossible.

143
00:08:36,799 --> 00:08:42,105
All of us randomly chose the teacups
that we liked from the cupboard.

144
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,108
It would be quite impossible
to predict which cup...

145
00:08:45,208 --> 00:08:47,310
...the Director would choose
and put cyanide inside just that one.

146
00:08:47,544 --> 00:08:50,380
If their forecast was off even a little,
then someone else would have died.

147
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,382
That's true...

148
00:08:54,017 --> 00:08:56,419
Well? How is that woman?

149
00:08:56,486 --> 00:08:59,222
She's resting soundly.

150
00:09:07,697 --> 00:09:09,666
I wonder what her intentions are?

151
00:09:09,899 --> 00:09:13,570
Losing consciousness like that
just as soon as her husband died.

152
00:09:14,337 --> 00:09:16,539
Wasn't it you?

153
00:09:16,673 --> 00:09:17,840
The one who killed the Director.

154
00:09:17,907 --> 00:09:19,142
Why would I do that?

155
00:09:19,242 --> 00:09:20,743
I know that.

156
00:09:20,810 --> 00:09:23,646
Neither you nor I had a motive to.

157
00:09:24,981 --> 00:09:27,550
There's only one person here with a motive.

158
00:09:27,617 --> 00:09:28,718
"Evil Woman"

159
00:09:28,785 --> 00:09:31,154
The one who couldn't forgive
her husband for having an affair...

160
00:09:31,254 --> 00:09:33,389
Chisato-san?

161
00:09:34,157 --> 00:09:36,993
Didn't she put cyanide on that sugar cube?

162
00:09:37,060 --> 00:09:38,628
"Ponisshu sugar cubes..."

163
00:09:39,162 --> 00:09:44,801
But, the one who drank the Director's tea first
was Chisato-san herself, wasn't it?

164
00:09:44,867 --> 00:09:47,804
If she had put the cyanide
in the center of the sugar cube...

165
00:09:47,904 --> 00:09:49,806
...and then drank from the cup before it melted,
she'd be fine, wouldn't she?

166
00:09:49,872 --> 00:09:51,608
But didn't she expressly stir it?

167
00:09:51,641 --> 00:09:53,876
Even if it was a little later,
she would've died herself.

168
00:09:53,977 --> 00:09:55,878
That would be too dangerous, wouldn't it?

169
00:09:57,614 --> 00:09:58,881
Collagen time!

170
00:09:59,048 --> 00:10:00,350
Collagen?

171
00:10:00,416 --> 00:10:04,454
I have to take it at regular times.
An actresses' life is her skin, isn't it?

172
00:10:05,355 --> 00:10:08,091
Is this the sort of time to be taking that?

173
00:10:08,658 --> 00:10:10,026
What is this?

174
00:10:16,933 --> 00:10:18,434
It's potassium cyanide!

175
00:10:18,468 --> 00:10:19,502
- Eh?
- Eh?

176
00:10:19,869 --> 00:10:23,039
Why would potassium cyanide
be in Saori-san's purse...

177
00:10:23,139 --> 00:10:24,073
Are you the criminal?

178
00:10:24,107 --> 00:10:25,575
Don't even joke about that!

179
00:10:25,675 --> 00:10:27,577
That isn't my purse!

180
00:10:28,077 --> 00:10:29,345
This is.

181
00:10:29,445 --> 00:10:31,214
This one's mine.

182
00:10:31,314 --> 00:10:32,749
That's that woman's purse.

183
00:10:32,882 --> 00:10:34,283
Why is this?

184
00:10:34,384 --> 00:10:37,987
I asked the Director for a purse, so he
bought me one the same as that woman's.

185
00:10:38,287 --> 00:10:40,657
He thought it'd be funny
if I showed up with it.

186
00:10:40,757 --> 00:10:42,225
With that...

187
00:10:42,325 --> 00:10:45,828
I guess the criminal is Chisato-san?

188
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:49,232
Ah, Ma'am.

189
00:10:52,869 --> 00:10:54,237
"Ma'am?"

190
00:11:03,112 --> 00:11:05,448
Where am I?

191
00:11:07,917 --> 00:11:11,421
Who... are you people?

192
00:11:16,793 --> 00:11:20,697
You really don't remember anything?

193
00:11:22,565 --> 00:11:25,268
She's also forgotten her own name...

194
00:11:28,004 --> 00:11:30,440
When a person receives a big enough shock...

195
00:11:30,540 --> 00:11:33,209
...I've heard that they can lose their memories.

196
00:11:33,376 --> 00:11:38,414
The sensation of not wanting to remember
blocks off all memories of the past.

197
00:11:38,848 --> 00:11:40,316
It seems to be a kind of defense instinct.

198
00:11:40,416 --> 00:11:42,251
She's play-acting!

199
00:11:42,585 --> 00:11:46,689
Isn't it a little too convenient to have
committed a murder and then lost her memory?

200
00:11:46,889 --> 00:11:47,924
Murder?

201
00:11:47,957 --> 00:11:48,991
Saori-san!

202
00:11:49,025 --> 00:11:52,295
I'll tear this lying woman's mask off!

203
00:12:01,838 --> 00:12:04,040
Here are your true colors!

204
00:12:04,107 --> 00:12:06,175
"'Femme fatale' Nagata Chisato"
Go on! Take a good, hard look!

205
00:12:06,509 --> 00:12:09,178
You put your own adultery off on a shelf while
saying you can't allow your husband's adultery.

206
00:12:09,278 --> 00:12:11,714
You killed your husband
for your own selfish reasons.

207
00:12:11,748 --> 00:12:13,783
You're a devil woman!

208
00:12:14,016 --> 00:12:15,084
Lies...

209
00:12:15,151 --> 00:12:17,286
Just how far do you intend to
go on feigning ignorance?!

210
00:12:17,720 --> 00:12:21,157
You were always putting on these
performances in order to trick the Director!

211
00:12:21,224 --> 00:12:23,693
The Director was saying you'd even act in bed.

212
00:12:23,793 --> 00:12:26,996
You may be intending to escape from this crime
by saying you don't remember anything...

213
00:12:27,096 --> 00:12:30,066
...but I will never allow that to happen!

214
00:12:30,133 --> 00:12:32,769
Act properly and confess!

215
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,604
You lying bitch!

216
00:12:37,406 --> 00:12:38,841
Stop it...

217
00:12:38,875 --> 00:12:40,643
Stop it...

218
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:43,379
Stop it...

219
00:12:45,581 --> 00:12:48,851
Have you really lost your memories?

220
00:12:56,058 --> 00:12:58,795
Ran, Kudo-kun, a moment.

221
00:13:04,967 --> 00:13:08,304
I think I know the man she was with here.

222
00:13:08,838 --> 00:13:10,506
You know him?

223
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:12,475
Yeah. Kimura Keisuke.

224
00:13:12,775 --> 00:13:14,911
He was an actor with a small theater group...

225
00:13:15,077 --> 00:13:18,247
...who committed suicide 2 months after
this magazine was published.

226
00:13:18,648 --> 00:13:19,916
Suicide?!

227
00:13:20,049 --> 00:13:22,852
A famous actress and totally unknown actor.

228
00:13:22,919 --> 00:13:25,288
No matter how you look at it,
they're unbalanced, aren't they?

229
00:13:25,421 --> 00:13:29,158
That's why even if Chisato-san tempted
some hot young man to kill her boredom...

230
00:13:29,258 --> 00:13:32,728
...rumors are she abandoned him in the end.

231
00:13:32,895 --> 00:13:35,565
Was that the reason why he committed suicide?

232
00:13:35,665 --> 00:13:36,999
"'Femme fatale' Nagata Chisato"

233
00:13:37,099 --> 00:13:39,702
Shin'ichi? Why are you taking a photo?

234
00:13:53,449 --> 00:13:55,017
"Evil Woman"

235
00:14:09,732 --> 00:14:14,103
I thought by doing this,
I might remember a little something.

236
00:14:20,643 --> 00:14:23,279
Have you remembered anything?

237
00:14:23,946 --> 00:14:27,049
No, nothing.

238
00:14:35,091 --> 00:14:37,526
I wonder what this room is?

239
00:14:38,661 --> 00:14:41,197
Do you want to see inside?

240
00:14:41,631 --> 00:14:42,999
Yes.

241
00:14:58,147 --> 00:15:00,049
My husband's room?

242
00:15:01,017 --> 00:15:03,920
I wonder what sort of person
my husband was.

243
00:15:06,022 --> 00:15:07,890
What did he do?

244
00:15:08,157 --> 00:15:09,892
He was a movie director.

245
00:15:10,893 --> 00:15:13,696
Movie... director...

246
00:15:31,247 --> 00:15:32,949
This is...

247
00:15:33,749 --> 00:15:36,285
This is the rehearsal hall.

248
00:15:36,519 --> 00:15:39,422
Director Nagata would gather his staff...

249
00:15:39,522 --> 00:15:43,526
...and, before he would shoot, he would
have them rehearse here without fail.

250
00:15:43,993 --> 00:15:46,562
Of course, you as well.

251
00:15:47,563 --> 00:15:48,965
Me, too?

252
00:15:49,165 --> 00:15:50,299
Yes.

253
00:15:55,471 --> 00:15:57,974
Ah... I can't...

254
00:15:59,208 --> 00:16:01,277
I can't remember anything...

255
00:16:04,547 --> 00:16:06,949
"There are no mistakes in her behavior..."

256
00:16:07,550 --> 00:16:09,051
"Is it acting?"

257
00:16:09,318 --> 00:16:11,687
"Or else is it real..."

258
00:16:40,816 --> 00:16:43,753
"Summer... Storm..."

259
00:16:45,187 --> 00:16:49,458
That was the first work you
and Director Nagata made together.

260
00:16:59,902 --> 00:17:03,439
This is... my husband...

261
00:17:03,739 --> 00:17:08,544
In these photos,
I seem to be having a lot of fun.

262
00:17:10,146 --> 00:17:11,847
Sad, isn't it...

263
00:17:12,648 --> 00:17:17,019
Not being able to remember
such fun memories.

264
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:23,325
Um...

265
00:17:23,626 --> 00:17:26,595
Did I really murder my husband?

266
00:17:28,764 --> 00:17:30,566
If that's so...

267
00:17:31,467 --> 00:17:34,370
Then I'm afraid of myself...

268
00:17:47,016 --> 00:17:50,920
"A AUK KEEN SKI."
What does this mean...

269
00:17:50,986 --> 00:17:52,621
"Glegle Translate"

270
00:17:52,755 --> 00:17:55,257
"Sea sparrow's sharp ski."

271
00:17:56,425 --> 00:17:58,160
Try the other one...

272
00:17:58,861 --> 00:18:03,499
"A AUK KEEN SKI."
What does this mean...

273
00:18:03,899 --> 00:18:06,836
"Sea sparrow seeks ink."

274
00:18:09,105 --> 00:18:10,573
It's an anagram!

275
00:18:10,806 --> 00:18:13,242
The great detective's worried.

276
00:18:13,609 --> 00:18:15,311
Be quiet.

277
00:18:17,079 --> 00:18:21,851
You don't have a clue for either the motive,
the criminal or their method of killing.

278
00:18:21,951 --> 00:18:23,752
I do know two of them.

279
00:18:23,986 --> 00:18:25,387
Eh? You do know?

280
00:18:25,488 --> 00:18:26,956
All that's left is...

281
00:18:27,323 --> 00:18:29,258
...the method of killing.

282
00:18:49,011 --> 00:18:50,880
I see...

283
00:18:51,147 --> 00:18:53,516
That's how it was!

284
00:18:54,617 --> 00:18:55,684
Eh?

285
00:18:55,985 --> 00:18:57,686
I've seen it.

286
00:18:58,320 --> 00:19:01,123
The one and only truth.

287
00:19:27,716 --> 00:19:30,219
Were you intending to erase the evidence?

288
00:19:31,620 --> 00:19:36,792
The one who killed Director Nagata
with potassium cyanide... was you, wasn't it?

289
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:41,897
Ishihara Kana-san.

290
00:19:43,999 --> 00:19:45,834
What is this foolishness...

291
00:19:46,135 --> 00:19:49,805
What reason would I have to kill Director Nagata?

292
00:19:49,972 --> 00:19:53,776
The one you were holding a grudge
against wasn't Director Nagata...

293
00:19:53,876 --> 00:19:56,845
...but his wife, Chisato-san.

294
00:20:01,617 --> 00:20:03,118
Kana-san.

295
00:20:03,552 --> 00:20:07,423
Wasn't the man who appeared in this
weekly magazine along with Chisato-san...

296
00:20:07,756 --> 00:20:10,259
...actually your lover?

297
00:20:11,093 --> 00:20:12,962
Kimura Keisuke.

298
00:20:14,096 --> 00:20:20,035
You have on the same good-luck bracelet
that Keisuke-san has in this magazine.

299
00:20:20,102 --> 00:20:23,272
With only that, how could you call us lovers...

300
00:20:23,839 --> 00:20:27,843
On the faceplate of both bracelets
are inscribed some characters of the alphabet.

301
00:20:28,310 --> 00:20:32,448
On Keisuke-san's it's, "A AUK KEEN SKI."

302
00:20:32,781 --> 00:20:36,552
On yours it's, "A AUK SEEK INK."

303
00:20:36,785 --> 00:20:39,555
These are anagrams...

304
00:20:39,655 --> 00:20:42,391
...where if you change the arrangement of
the characters, you create a different meaning.

305
00:20:42,424 --> 00:20:46,495
When you analyze the
11 characters in these anagrams...

306
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:50,099
...you get "Keisuke Kana."

307
00:20:50,232 --> 00:20:54,136
In other words, both of your names.

308
00:20:54,603 --> 00:20:56,205
Both of your names.

309
00:20:57,473 --> 00:21:01,644
You figured you wanted to
take revenge on Chisato-san...

310
00:21:01,877 --> 00:21:04,613
...who had driven your lover
Keisuke-san into suicide.

311
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:09,551
Your intended revenge
wasn't to kill Chisato-san...

312
00:21:09,718 --> 00:21:13,589
...but to place the stigma
of being called a murderer on her.

313
00:21:13,722 --> 00:21:16,825
So you tried to kill Director Nagata...

314
00:21:16,992 --> 00:21:20,729
...and then pin the blame
for it on Chisato-san.

315
00:21:21,797 --> 00:21:23,465
How?

316
00:21:24,600 --> 00:21:27,369
Are you saying I placed
the potassium cyanide in the tea?

317
00:21:27,503 --> 00:21:31,073
The potassium cyanide wasn't put in the tea.

318
00:21:31,807 --> 00:21:35,778
It was applied to all of the cups beforehand.

319
00:21:35,911 --> 00:21:37,780
What's more...

320
00:21:37,913 --> 00:21:41,650
...it was applied along this portion of the cups.

321
00:21:42,017 --> 00:21:45,754
But, by applying cyanide
to the right hand side only...

322
00:21:46,588 --> 00:21:50,793
...along this section on the opposite side,
mouths wouldn't touch it.

323
00:21:50,926 --> 00:21:56,165
That way, even if Chisato-san
did taste the Director's tea...

324
00:21:56,632 --> 00:21:58,267
...she wouldn't die.

325
00:22:01,503 --> 00:22:04,807
You normally hold a cup with
your dominant hand, don't you?

326
00:22:05,474 --> 00:22:09,945
Director Nagata was
the only member of our party...

327
00:22:10,312 --> 00:22:11,880
...who was left-handed.

328
00:22:12,348 --> 00:22:15,918
You casually checked us out about that.

329
00:22:20,022 --> 00:22:23,225
From the start you knew
which was Chisato-san's dominant hand.

330
00:22:23,525 --> 00:22:28,163
So whichever cup he would
eventually take from the cupboard...

331
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:32,568
...the result was that only Director Nagata
would end up taking the potassium cyanide.

332
00:22:32,935 --> 00:22:35,938
The one who switched those purses
was also you, wasn't it?

333
00:22:36,138 --> 00:22:41,944
So that Saori-san would make the mistake of
finding the cyanide in Chisato-san's purse.

334
00:22:42,111 --> 00:22:47,249
Your finishing touch was to have been
wiping the cyanide off all the cups.

335
00:22:52,588 --> 00:22:54,656
I got so far.

336
00:22:56,125 --> 00:23:01,397
Yes, it's just as you say.

337
00:23:06,602 --> 00:23:08,437
This woman...

338
00:23:09,104 --> 00:23:13,442
...was the instigator who toyed with
Keisuke's dream and who drove him to his death!

339
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:16,111
Keisuke...

340
00:23:17,012 --> 00:23:19,915
...was so thrilled when he
contacted me to say...

341
00:23:20,549 --> 00:23:23,385
...that you had promised him
a co-starring role.

342
00:23:25,988 --> 00:23:28,223
Yet even so, you broke that promise...

343
00:23:28,290 --> 00:23:32,327
...and then abandoned Keisuke like
he was some worn-out dust cloth!

344
00:23:33,462 --> 00:23:35,330
That's why Keisuke...

345
00:23:35,697 --> 00:23:39,902
...despaired about everything and chose death.
He had no choice but to choose that!

346
00:23:42,171 --> 00:23:44,606
I swore revenge.

347
00:23:45,641 --> 00:23:49,044
That worthless woman must die.

348
00:23:49,178 --> 00:23:52,548
Nevertheless, you went and had amnesia.

349
00:23:53,081 --> 00:23:55,617
When a person has lost their memories...

350
00:23:56,785 --> 00:23:59,721
...pining a crime on them has no meaning.

351
00:24:02,291 --> 00:24:07,196
You'd never suffer for all the sins
you had committed in the past.

352
00:24:13,836 --> 00:24:16,872
What on earth was this for...

353
00:24:18,941 --> 00:24:20,275
No.

354
00:24:20,576 --> 00:24:25,414
I think you achieved your goal perfectly.

355
00:24:25,647 --> 00:24:27,983
Your purpose was to a least..

356
00:24:28,617 --> 00:24:33,388
...make her conscious of her past crimes.

357
00:24:33,622 --> 00:24:35,057
Chisato-san...

358
00:24:35,424 --> 00:24:39,094
...your amnesia is a fake, isn't it?

359
00:24:39,428 --> 00:24:40,863
Chisato-san...

360
00:24:41,196 --> 00:24:45,234
...your amnesia is a fake, isn't it?

361
00:24:48,770 --> 00:24:52,407
When you entered the pitch-black darkness
of that basement warehouse...

362
00:24:52,875 --> 00:24:55,911
...you didn't hesitate in turning on the lights.

363
00:25:00,282 --> 00:25:02,518
Why, if you had amnesia...

364
00:25:02,651 --> 00:25:07,155
...would you know the location of
that room's light switch?

365
00:25:10,559 --> 00:25:13,729
I didn't think you had noticed.

366
00:25:14,830 --> 00:25:16,798
But why...

367
00:25:17,032 --> 00:25:18,934
...did you put on this amnesia act?

368
00:25:19,034 --> 00:25:22,437
When I woke up, here in this room...

369
00:25:22,905 --> 00:25:27,175
...all of you were making a fuss over
finding the cyanide.

370
00:25:27,442 --> 00:25:32,281
"With that...
I guess the criminal is Chisato-san?"

371
00:25:32,347 --> 00:25:34,483
I had a hunch.

372
00:25:34,883 --> 00:25:39,254
That someone was trying to
pin the guilt for the murder on me.

373
00:25:39,755 --> 00:25:45,360
So I thought by feigning amnesia
I might find out who the murderer was.

374
00:25:46,094 --> 00:25:47,596
But...

375
00:25:47,863 --> 00:25:52,935
...since you saw through me,
I guess my acting still has a ways to go yet.

376
00:25:57,105 --> 00:26:01,076
Kana-san, shall I tell you?

377
00:26:01,410 --> 00:26:05,147
The reason why
I broke my promise with Keisuke.

378
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:11,186
He had no talent as an actor.

379
00:26:11,353 --> 00:26:13,155
It's just that simple.

380
00:26:14,389 --> 00:26:17,559
For you to have murdered for that man's sake...

381
00:26:17,893 --> 00:26:20,529
...just makes you a foolish woman.

382
00:26:22,631 --> 00:26:25,734
Still, I'm grateful to you.

383
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:32,007
I was thinking it would be best if
my husband was dead.

384
00:26:33,408 --> 00:26:38,847
Because he had already become
an unnecessary person in my life.

385
00:26:42,284 --> 00:26:43,685
Thank you.

386
00:26:44,219 --> 00:26:46,355
I should have killed you...

387
00:26:46,955 --> 00:26:49,625
You're the one I should have killed!

388
00:26:53,729 --> 00:26:55,797
You're the lowest of women.

389
00:26:56,732 --> 00:26:58,600
I think so, too.

390
00:26:58,700 --> 00:27:00,068
Me, too!

391
00:27:01,737 --> 00:27:03,805
I don't mind.

392
00:27:04,339 --> 00:27:06,875
I can be an actress like that.

393
00:27:20,756 --> 00:27:22,190
Still...

394
00:27:22,357 --> 00:27:26,228
How could the criminal behind this know
that was the last day I had tea?!

395
00:27:26,328 --> 00:27:28,797
They must have been observing you
for a long time now.

396
00:27:28,897 --> 00:27:31,967
Is it true the criminal's been watching us?

397
00:27:32,067 --> 00:27:33,969
Probably.

398
00:27:45,981 --> 00:27:48,116
"Actress"

399
00:27:53,588 --> 00:27:56,024
I already have a bad
premonition about this one...

400
00:27:56,124 --> 00:27:58,193
Doesn't seem to be over yet...

401
00:27:58,326 --> 00:28:00,762
Let's get going! Go on!

402
00:28:16,745 --> 00:28:17,879
Ow!

403
00:28:17,946 --> 00:28:19,114
What is it?!

404
00:28:19,381 --> 00:28:22,350
Somehow... my body's gone numb...

405
00:28:22,484 --> 00:28:23,985
- Ran!
- Ran!

406
00:28:24,086 --> 00:28:25,821
Oi, are you okay?!

407
00:28:35,297 --> 00:28:40,068
"If not given an antidote in time..."

408
00:28:40,302 --> 00:28:42,070
"...she will die."

409
00:28:50,378 --> 00:28:51,446
Damn!

410
00:28:51,480 --> 00:28:53,048
What day is this?!

411
00:28:53,215 --> 00:28:55,250
What should we input?!

412
00:28:55,417 --> 00:28:58,386
Oi, boy detective!
Hurry and remember!

413
00:28:58,787 --> 00:29:00,756
Wait, Ran...

414
00:29:01,990 --> 00:29:03,325
That's it!

415
00:29:03,625 --> 00:29:05,160
This is...

416
00:29:05,327 --> 00:29:07,929
That incident at the cabaret club...

417
00:29:12,768 --> 00:29:16,805
"The Murder Play Surrounding
the No.1 Cabaret Girls"

